date,area,claimed,was_true,caught_by,lesson
日期,範圍,我當時的說法,實際情況,被什麼抓到,教訓
2026-08-27,Swift concurrency,"nonisolated(unsafe) on a local fixes a sending error","It does for a reference being passed along; not for a closure's type, nor for a value whose region holds isolated state","The same error reappearing at the same line, twice","Three encounters before the rule was clear. Annotate the type, not the local, when the region is the problem."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"A WinUI sweep can show almost nothing beyond launch","The desktop fallback photographs the window perfectly; P8's capture showed the scroll its action file performs","Actually opening the capture instead of reasoning about it","Look at the artefact before writing what it can prove."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"P4's gtk4 build failure is a regression","P4 is the WinUI escape-hatch app; canImport(WinUIBackend) is true even under -gtk4","Its WinUI build passing in the same run","A FAIL next to a PASS on the same app is a question, not a finding."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"P20 exits before the capture, so P20 has a defect","The wait was 14 s; P20's action file holds 16.8 s of sleeps","Its log had `replaying` and no `replayed`","When one item of twenty-four fails, suspect the harness's constant first."
2026-08-27,Tooling,"MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*' with tasklist //FI","tasklist needs the doubled slash and NO exclusion; taskkill needs the opposite","Every app reporting launch failure with its window on screen","Already written in memory. Reading it is not the same as checking it."
2026-08-27,Process,"A sed one-liner is fine for a two-line rename in a scratch file","It happened to be right","Noticing afterwards, not before","The rule says every file change goes through Edit. Convenience is exactly when it gets broken."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"Adding six targets to migratedToSwift6 after measuring four","Gtk had two errors on Windows and broke every gtk4 app build","A P8 build failing in the sweep, not a targeted build","Measure each target before listing it. The list is cheap to extend one name at a time."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"A typo guard on migratedToSwift6 is pure safety","It rejected GtkBackend on Windows, where SCUI_HOST_BACKENDS_ONLY deletes that target before the check","Its first real use","A guard that has never fired has never been tested."
2026-08-27,Audit,"ButtonStyle, LabelStyle, ShapeStyle and ToggleStyle are all absent","ToggleStyle has one declaration and ten references","Reading Toggle.swift for another reason","The grep was piped through head -10. Count, do not sample, when the claim is 'none'."
2026-08-27,Sweep design,"One script can build and drive every app","The build gaps are idle time; the workstation locked itself out at the second app","The run itself","Split work by what it needs from the environment, not by what it is about."
2026-08-27,Swift generics,"Shadow `backend` with the cast result","The existential does not satisfy BaseAppBackend","Twenty conformance errors at once","A cast that narrows can also lose what the caller already had."
2026-08-27,Measurement,"eval getwindowgeometry --shell then eval getmouselocation --shell","The second overwrote X and Y, so the probe compared the cursor with itself","Every offset coming out 0,0","A clean null result from a probe is a reason to check the probe."
2026-08-27,Environment,"Awake can run however it likes","Its console window sat in the middle of the screen, over the desktop captures the WinUI pass depends on","Seeing it in a capture","A tool added to help the test is part of the test."
2026-08-26,Performance,"WSL is 3-4x faster than Windows for this project's builds","Windows is 3.3x faster for a full build; WSL is 9.5x faster for a no-op","A clean measurement of both","Two different questions were being answered by one number."
2026-08-26,Performance,"-gtk4 is slower because Gtk is a big module","130 s versus 123 s, 5% apart; the 118 s was mtime churn","Measuring instead of explaining","An explanation that arrives before the measurement usually survives it."
2026-08-26,UI testing,"P24 and P20 stop receiving clicks","The coordinates were measured on a capture the file's own earlier steps had invalidated","Retracting it twice before finding the pattern","A step that changes the layout must be the last step that uses that layout's coordinates."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"swift build -Xswiftc -swift-version -Xswiftc 6 measures the language mode","It is global, so it recompiled dependencies; all 17 errors were in swift-image-formats","None of the errors naming our own files","Size a per-target job with the per-target mechanism."
2026-08-27,Swift 6,"SwiftCrossUI's one error needs a decision about the protocols","Two nonisolated keywords, and the cause was in BaseStubs rather than in the type the diagnostic named","Trying the fixes the diagnostic implied and watching them fail","The error names where it surfaced, not where it came from."
2026-08-27,Tooling,"csv2 -r emits tab-separated fields, so awk -F tab can pivot it","It emits CSV, quoting and all",Checking with od -c before trusting the pivot,The first version would have mis-parsed every row and produced a plausible empty matrix.
2026-08-27,Shell,grep -c prints 0 on no match so a || fallback is harmless,"It prints 0 AND exits 1, so both fired and the count became the two characters 0\n0",An integer comparison failing on a count,"A fallback for a case the tool already handles is a second answer, not a safety net."
2026-08-27,Review,"An agent reported my sweep evidence was invalid, and it sounded right","The sweep never used the broken function; same script, same grep, gave 16 ok on gtk4 and no line on WinUI",Checking whether sweep_drive.zsh references test_common.zsh at all -- it does not,A correct bug report can carry an incorrect consequence. Verify the consequence separately from the bug.
2026-08-27,Environment,The screen lock came from the sign-in timeout the user had already raised to 3 hours,It came from the screen saver: ScreenSaveTimeOut 600 with ScreenSaverIsSecure 1,Reading the registry instead of trusting the settings page,Windows has four independent things that lock a screen. Name which one before advising a change.
2026-08-27,UI testing,allowsHitTesting(false) does not block a click on GtkBackend -- P10 expects Hidden clicks 0 and gets 1,"1 is the working value. The modifier means the top layer does not take hits, so the click reaches the button below, which is what SwiftUI does. 0 is what a no-op produces",Replacing setHitTesting with a no-op and watching the counter fall to 0,A counter that moves is not automatically a failure. Establish which direction means working before filing it.
2026-08-27,Windows input,"Keyboard action files cannot run at all on Windows, so AttachThreadInput is needed",They already ran. The HWND_TOPMOST pin added after the task was filed had fixed it; P10 quit on Ctrl-Q with the new code and without it,Running the control -- the version without AttachThreadInput behaved identically,A task description is a claim with a date on it. Re-run the failure before writing the fix.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"The popover background after the fix is rgb(53,53,53), so the theme paints it now",The menu never opened. That was the window background -- the action file clicked before layout settled and missed silently,"Cropping the capture and looking at it, because the number was suspiciously tidy",A measurement of the wrong pixels reads exactly like a result. Confirm the thing being measured is on screen.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"Enabled and disabled WinUI buttons both have fill rgb(32,32,32)",The window moves between launches; those coordinates were outside it entirely,"Both fills matching, where the previous run had 45 and 42",Pixel coordinates expire when the window is relaunched. Locate the window in every capture before sampling it.
2026-08-28,Review,border: none plus box-shadow: none removes the GTK entry focus ring -- an agent sweep ranked this severity 5,"GTK 4 draws the ring with outline, which this backend never sets. Measured present at rgb(36,80,133), 196px wide",Measuring the focused and unfocused fields before repeating the claim,"A plausible mechanism is not a measurement. Check the mechanism, not only the symptom."
2026-08-28,Review,The TextEditor disabled state is hidden by its unconditional background: none -- from the same agent sweep,"The symptom was real, the cause was not. It was the forced foreground colour; fixing that alone restored the dimming, 255 to 145","A/B against HEAD by swapping the backend file, rather than reasoning from the report","A correct symptom can carry a wrong cause. Fix what the A/B shows, not what the report says."
2026-08-28,Measurement,"The popover change is unverifiable here -- Adwaita is identical before and after, so there is nothing to show","Under GTK_THEME=HighContrast the old code drew a dark rgb(44,44,44) menu on a white rgb(253,253,252) window, in the theme people pick because they need contrast",Trying the other theme instead of concluding from the default one,A no-op under the default configuration is not evidence of no effect. Vary the input the code actually branches on.
2026-08-28,Attribution,"Standing the GtkBackend isControl background down fixes #390, since disabled buttons come out distinct","The disabled-to-enabled gap survived both ways, 5 units versus 10. What the enforcement actually destroyed was the border",Measuring the two states instead of reading the screenshot,Do not attach a known issue to a change because the screenshot looks better.
2026-08-28,Review,"modelbutton is missing from the opacity: 0.5 disabled rule, so disabled menu items read as enabled","modelbutton IS missing and it does not matter -- GTK dims an insensitive menu item through its label colour without the rule. The real cause was the popover CSS forcing a flat colour over the theme, already fixed hours earlier","Building the instrument P20 never had, then A/B-ing it against the pre-fix backend",Two plausible causes for one symptom. The one that names a missing line of CSS is the more convincing and was the wrong one.
2026-08-28,Measurement,"Pre-fix menu labels measured 53,53,53 and 255,255,255 -- so the disabled item was BRIGHTER than the enabled one","Those rows were sampled from a window that had moved between launches. Read off the image, all three were 255,255,255",The numbers being impossible -- an enabled label darker than the menu background,Same window-moved error as twice earlier today. An impossible number is a gift; a merely surprising one is the danger.
2026-08-28,Tooling,"Tallied the coverage matrix by piping csv2 --json into Python, and read off 45 RUN / 13 BUILT per platform","The tally was of surrogate-escaped byte soup -- every emoji comparison failed, so the counts were of unrecognised strings. The file itself is valid UTF-8; od -c gives E2 9C 85 for the tick",The status names printing as surrogate escapes instead of RUN or BUILT,"Windows ACP here is 950 and Python 3.14 leaves UTF-8 mode off, so a piped script inherits the locale for stdin and stdout rather than the file encoding. PYTHONUTF8=1 fixes it -- but csv2 -contains --filter listed the same rows with no Python at all, so the bug came of reaching past the tool that was already correct."
2026-08-28,Tooling,"Counted the coverage matrix at 107 records, by grepping csv2 --json output for the substring fields","104. The opening meta line carries a fields key holding the FIELD count (10), so a substring grep matches it as well as every record -- an over-count of exactly one, which reads as an off-by-one in my own edit rather than a bad method. csv2 already emits records:104 in its trailing meta, and csv2 -r piped to wc -l agrees","The number failing to move by exactly 1 across a single append, then counting three ways","Do not count JSON Lines by grepping a key: the same key appeared at two levels meaning two different things. csv2 answers the question itself. Its --help describes --json in five words and mentions neither the meta lines nor the records count, so this is also a csv2 doc gap."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Scanned menu rows for a separator by flagging every row whose dominant colour changed, and read the result as a list of candidates","That flags every row containing text, because glyphs break the dominant-colour run. It buried the one row that mattered. Then the same scan on a second run reported rgb(53,53,53) rows that were the window background, because the window had moved and the fixed coordinates missed the popover entirely",The colour being the window background rather than anything in a menu -- and it was the fourth window-moved miss in two days,"Define the signal before scanning for it. A separator is a row whose dominant colour spans the FULL width AND differs from the background; locate the popover by its own colour first, never by coordinates from a previous run."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Measured P39 cell means and got saturation 0 and saturation 2.5 identical, then reported deltas around 20 for six effects","Impossible on its face -- opposite effects cannot share a mean. The sample boxes sat at different relative offsets INSIDE their cells, and the gradient is conic, so each offset sees a different mix of hues. Re-measured at identical offsets: five of six were delta exactly 0.0",Two effects with opposite meanings returning the same number,"Anchor a sample to the thing being measured, not to the screen. Locate the cell, then sample the same relative window inside every one."
2026-08-29,Measurement,Mean cell colour is enough to tell whether a visual effect was applied,"It cannot see a blur at all -- averaging is what a blur does, so the mean is preserved. GTK blur measured delta 2.3 by mean and would have been filed as a no-op; by text edge energy it is 53.21 -> 1.76, a 30x drop, and plainly applied","P39 own header saying the text is the only thing with edges, read after the number looked wrong","Choose the metric from what the effect DOES. A single metric that cannot distinguish applied from dropped is not a weak test, it is a wrong answer."
2026-08-29,Diagnosis,"GTK 4.22.4 cannot render a transformed widget at all -- filed as a platform defect after ruling out four causes, one of which was the renderer","There is no GL renderer on this machine to have ruled out. GTK cannot realize it (OpenGL requires Direct Composition) and silently falls back to software GskCairoRenderer, which is the thing that cannot draw a transform node. GDK_DEBUG=dcomp gets GskGLRenderer and every transform renders correctly, hotpink 47873 -> 0","Five GSK_RENDERER values returning byte-identical 47873 -- five renderers cannot agree to the pixel, so they were one renderer five times","A control that silently degrades to the thing it was meant to be compared against proves nothing. Verify the alternative was actually used, not merely requested."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"Wrote the probe that re-enables the GTK transform, ran it, got 0 hotpink and nearly recorded that the bug was gone","The probe emitted matrix(..., 40px, 20px). CSS matrix() takes <number>, so px made the declaration invalid and GTK dropped it silently. Nothing was transformed and the tiles were still 90x57",Checking the tile geometry rather than trusting the count -- a probe that fails to apply looks exactly like a fixed bug,"When a test can pass for two reasons, one of them being that it never ran, measure the thing that distinguishes them every time."
2026-08-29,Tooling,"Put new backend code in a new file, Sources/GtkBackend/GtkBackend+GpuPreference.swift, and spent several builds debugging why the symbol was not found","The file was never compiled. Proven with a #error inside it that never fired, while edits to EXISTING files in the same directory took effect in the same build. Touching Package.swift to force a re-plan did not help. Moving the identical code into GtkBackend.swift compiled first time",The #error not firing -- the only test that separates not-compiled from compiles-but-wrong,"CAUSE STILL UNKNOWN, and recorded as unknown rather than guessed. Under testapp/compile.zsh a NEW .swift file under Sources/ may not enter the build; add code to an existing file, or verify with a temporary #error before debugging anything else."
2026-08-29,Diagnosis,"Deleting .build/debug.yaml did not make compile.zsh notice a new source file, so the cached build plan was ruled out","It was the right theory and the wrong directory. There are THREE work dirs -- .compile-work, .compile-work-gtk4, .compile-work-winui, one per backend -- and .gitignore documents them. The deletions hit .compile-work while -gtk4 builds in .compile-work-gtk4. Deleting the right one made the file compile immediately",Reading .gitignore for an unrelated reason and seeing the per-backend comment,"Ruling a theory out is a measurement too, and it fails the same way as any other: on the wrong target. Confirm the artefact being deleted is the one in use before concluding from its absence."
2026-08-29,Tooling,"Used taskkill //F //IM throughout, including inside a new zsh test script, having read the memory note that says taskkill needs the opposite slash treatment from tasklist","Under zsh it fails outright -- ERROR: Invalid argument/option - //F -- and the process SURVIVES. bash converts //F to /F and zsh does not, so the identical line works from the interactive shell and fails in a .zsh script. With stderr discarded it is completely silent, and the leftover GTK process then makes the next launch exit 0 with no window and no output","Four test cases reporting an empty log, then testing the kill directly instead of assuming it worked","tasklist wants the doubled slash, taskkill wants the single one. The memory said so and reading it was not the same as applying it -- the second time that exact sentence has been earned this week."
2026-08-29,Measurement,"The Windows GTK4 DLL contains zero GskVulkan symbols and does not import vulkan-1.dll, so the Vulkan renderer was never compiled in","The conclusion happened to be right and every step behind it was false. strings and objdump -p had been aimed at libgtk-4-1.dll, the MinGW name; this is an MSVC build and the file is gtk-4-1.dll. Both tools printed nothing for a file that does not exist, and neither treated that as an error, so nothing was read as zero. The real DLL does contain GskVulkanRenderer. The actual cause is gvsbuild passing -Dvulkan=disabled, which GSK_RENDERER=help reports directly","Running the same strings command for GskCairoRenderer, a name the runtime demonstrably prints, and getting 0 for that too","Grep first for a string that MUST be present. That control costs one line, and without it a count of zero cannot tell absent from unreadable. A file path is an input like any other and deserves the same suspicion as a flag."
2026-08-29,Review,"gpu_flag_test.zsh proved that the registry did not contain GpuPreference=5","The assertion used an empty expected string, and the shared check treats every string as containing empty text. That test would pass even if the registry query printed GpuPreference=5. The same review found the registry value path hardcoded to one checkout instead of deriving it from the output directory.",Reading the assertion rather than only its PASS output,"A negative assertion needs its own helper. Do not express absence as contains-empty, and derive registry paths from the executable under test."
2026-08-29,Review,"gpu_flag_test.zsh --no-build is safe to use with the existing P40.exe","It is safe only if that executable was built with SCUI_DEBUG=1. A non-debug-feature P40 treats -GPU list as ordinary app input and opens a window; the harness ran that case in the foreground, so it waited forever instead of reporting a failed precondition.",Rebuilding P40 without SCUI_DEBUG and then running the no-build harness,"A no-build option inherits the old binary's build flags. Either state the precondition or make the first check bounded so the wrong binary fails visibly."
2026-09-01,Verification,"The scale-factor change compiles -- committed it, pushed it, and said so in the commit message","It does not compile. addSignal is internal to the Gtk module, so GtkBackend cannot call it, and Gtk exposes no public equivalent. The build that reported exit 0 was run as `swift build ... | tail -6`, so the 0 was tails status and not the builds. The same shape happened twice more the same day: a wincap exit code read through a pipe, which turned a missing window into a success, and an mtime comparison written with --time-style=+%H:%M, which hid the date and made an 08-30 binary look newer than a 09-01 source","Rebuilding without a pipeline, after noticing the exe was older than the source it was supposedly built from","Never read $? after a pipeline -- it belongs to the last command, which is usually the one that cannot fail. Redirect to a file and read the real status, or use PIPESTATUS. This matters more for a build than for anything else, because a commit message asserts the build passed on the readers behalf, and here that assertion reached the remote."
2026-09-01,Build,Read exit code 0 from a compile.zsh wrapped in `nohup ... &` and treated the build as finished,"The 0 was the backgrounding itself. compile.zsh was still running ten minutes later, holding build.db; the exe timestamp had not moved and the log held only two pkg-config warnings","The next build failed with `database is locked ... two concurrent builds`, and `tasklist //FI` showed swift-build.exe alive","`&` returns 0 immediately, so an exit code taken from a backgrounded command says nothing about the command. Same family as reading `$?` after a pipeline. When a build must be backgrounded, print the wrapped command exit inside the background job (`cmd; printf exit=%d $?`) and verify the artefact timestamp moved -- this build was caught by the artefact, not by the status"
2026-09-02,Measurement,"Reported that testapp/compile.zsh exits 0 when swift build fails, and put it in two commit messages (b0a93243, 240fe18e) plus a task description","compile.zsh is correct: measured rc=1 on a deliberately broken P43, with 2 errors logged and the artefact mtime unmoved. zsh set -e does carry the status out, also measured","Re-running the probe as a script file written with the Write tool, instead of a quoted command line passed through wsl.exe","The `$?` was expanded by the OUTER shell before zsh ever ran. `wsl.exe -- bash -lc ...; echo $? > rc` bakes in the status of whatever ran BEFORE, so the file said 0 no matter what happened. Same family as the $var-eaten-crossing-wsl trap already recorded, but worse: that one empties a value and the script misbehaves visibly, this one substitutes a plausible number and the conclusion looks measured. Never read `$?` through a wsl.exe command line -- put the whole sequence in a script FILE and run that"
2026-09-02,Diagnosis,"Told the compiler error cannot find logger in scope meant logger was file-private to WinUIBackend.swift, removed two log calls to work around it, and wrote that reason into commit d0f2cb45","logger is a GLOBAL @_spi(Backends) public var in App.swift:14. The new file just used a plain `import SwiftCrossUI` instead of `@_spi(Backends) import SwiftCrossUI`, so the SPI was not in scope. Nothing was file-private","Reading App.swift while checking whether a static method could reach it -- a question that only came up later, by luck","Diagnosed from the error text without opening the declaration. `grep -n logger WinUIBackend.swift` showed uses but no definition, and no definition here was read as private to here rather than defined elsewhere. The cost was not the build error, which is loud, but the WORKAROUND: two diagnostics were deleted from a fallback path on a false premise, which is the silent part. Before removing code to satisfy a scope error, find the declaration -- `grep -rn var NAME` across the module, not just the file"
2026-09-02,Tooling,swift-bundler rejects the android SDK keys because the prebuilt binary is older than the vendored source; rebuilding will fix it,"All three binaries were byte-identical (sha256 bf07813b) and the submodule HEAD predates the build date, so the binary was already current. Upstream main rejected the keys too. The real cause was the spelling: the @Configuration macro converts minSDK to the TOML key min_sdk, so the file had been rejected whole since the day it was written",shasum on the three binaries and git log on the submodule -- both available before the first rebuild,Three rebuilds were spent on an unchecked premise. When an artefact and its source disagree compare them before rebuilding to reconcile them.
2026-09-02,Hit testing,allowsHitTesting(false) over a hidden button means Hidden clicks must stay 0,P10's own comment says the opposite -- the layer is opaque so only the modifier can let a click through and if the counter rises the click reached a button nobody could see which is the whole claim; macOS measures Direct 2 Covered 2 Hidden 2,Reading P10.swift before implementing rather than after -- the comment was four lines above the code I was already looking at,I wrote the expectation into the macOS action file from the modifier's name instead of from the app's stated claim and a subagent then inherited it. Read what the test says it is testing before writing down what it should report.
2026-09-02,csv2 editing,"Escaping a literal percent for csv2 the way printf needs it, writing 100%% <-> 200%% into a matrix note","csv2 takes its argument verbatim -- it is not a format string. The two characters were stored as-is, so the note now told the reader to cross from 100%% to 200%%. It parsed, it round-tripped, csv2 reported rc=0, and the row looked completely normal in every listing","Reading the field back with csv2 -get and grepping it for the doubled sign, as a deliberate check rather than by noticing it","A habit from one tool applied to another that only LOOKS similar. printf escaping is muscle memory and csv2 arguments are the same shape -- a quoted string full of text -- so nothing signals the switch. Check the destination tool contract, not the shape of the argument. Nothing errors when this is wrong; the damage is silent and lands in the data"
2026-09-02,csv2 reading,"A newly appended matrix row is corrupt -- awk with a comma separator shows its status column holding the words ""clipped to fill and to stroke"" instead of an emoji so the append shifted every field",The row was perfect and the CHECK was broken. awk split on a comma INSIDE the quoted item name so every column after it read one position early. csv2 -get 106:3 returns the emoji,Re-reading the same fields with csv2 -get instead of awk -- the project rule says csv2 files are read with csv2 and that is the rule I had just broken,A broken verification tool is indistinguishable from broken data and it fails in the more alarming direction: it INVENTS a defect. I nearly rewrote a correct row. The project already records that comma-splitting with awk or cut silently mis-splits quoted commas and shifts every column right of them; I applied that rule to the file I was editing but not to the command I checked it with. Verification code deserves the same rules as production code
2026-09-03,Measurement,"Showed a 393-point capture of P43 as evidence that the same staggering reproduces on macOS at phone width, and said so to the user","AppKit refuses to make that window smaller than 568 points -- its minimum comes from its content. The image was a 393-point CROP of a 568-point window, taken with screencapture -R. Nothing had been resized, so it was not evidence of anything","Reading the window size back with System Events after a resize that appeared to work: it answered 568, 700","A crop and a resize produce the same rectangle on screen and mean opposite things. When a capture is the evidence for a size claim, read the size back from the window rather than from the file you just wrote."
2026-09-03,Diagnosis,Wrote in bugs/bug-UIkit.md that a tap on a List row does not select on iOS,"P3 detail list selects on a tap and so does P7 own split view sidebar. Only P7 plain list did not, and the cause was not lists at all -- UIView.hitTest returns nil for a point outside a view own bounds before it looks at any subview, and P30 button failed the same way with no list in it","Trying a second app after the first, which cost one run",Generalised from one control in one app to a whole feature on a whole platform. A second sample was one replay away and would have prevented the entry being written.
2026-09-03,Diagnosis,Blamed synchronous touch delivery for blanking the Android window -- the view graph update running nested inside a block already on the main queue -- and changed the synthesiser to dispatch asynchronously,"It made no difference. The coordinate was wrong: 299 points at density 2.625 is 785 pixels, which is the tab row, not the 942 where Increment counter sits. Both taps had been pressing tab buttons, and pressing a tab button blanks the window on a real adb shell input tap too","A tap at the correctly derived coordinate, which produced counter: 1 with the page intact","Changed the mechanism before checking the input to it. On a platform where a wrong coordinate presses something else rather than erroring, derive the coordinate again before suspecting the machinery."
2026-09-03,Scope of a claim,The 39px content shortfall from gtk_window_set_default_size is a WSLg observation -- bugs/Gtk4-bugs.md section 5 framed it that way and I repeated it all session,Windows GTK does exactly the same. P16 with SCUI_DEBUG_SPLIT logs leadingContent 200x480 twice then 200x441 -- the identical 39. Only the decoration thickness differs between the two GTK platforms (frame +28/+29 on Windows against +0/+0 under WSLg); the shortfall does not,Measuring the second platform instead of reasoning about it. I had already written that the Windows frame was +28/+29 and inferred from that arithmetic that Windows GTK might be honouring the request -- the inference was wrong and one run settled it,"A defect measured on ONE platform gets written up as belonging to that platform. Nothing in the note was false; the scope was invented. This is the same shape as the Mac side generalising a List selection failure from one list to all of them and then correcting it. Where the code is shared -- and gtk_window_set_default_size is called from the same GtkBackend.createWindow on both -- the null hypothesis is that the behaviour is shared too. Name the platform you measured, not the platform you think is affected"
2026-09-04,Claim written from a name,"P23's action file claimed pressing ""More rows"" takes rows: 8 to rows: 9 -- one more row, which is what the button is called","It adds four. P23.swift:143 is rowCount + 4, and the replay measured 12. The app was right and the file was wrong","Replaying the file I had just written and reading the number, which did not match what I had asserted in it","A claim written from what a control is NAMED rather than from what its code DOES fails against a working build, and it fails in the direction that looks like a defect in the app. The fix is to read the source before writing the claim, not to loosen the claim afterwards. The file keeps both the wrong claim and the correction, because the shape is worth more than the number"
2026-09-04,Rationale never checked against the output,"P44's first version drew a blue rectangle at the frame's size behind the oversized child, with a paragraph explaining that this keeps the frame's own edges visible however far the child spills","The marker was invisible in every state. Clipped, the child covers the frame exactly; unclipped, it more than covers it. The paragraph described a picture the code could not produce",Looking at the first Android screenshot and not finding the blue anywhere,"I wrote the justification and the code in the same pass and checked neither against the other. A comment that explains why something is visible is a claim about the rendered output and has to be read against the rendered output. The replacement is a measurement -- 120x60 clipped, 200x100 not -- because a number can be checked without trusting the prose"
2026-09-04,Measurement predicate,P44 on macOS has no blue pixels anywhere in the window -- I reported zero and was about to call it an AppKit defect on that basis,"The predicate required green below 150 and macOS blue is (78, 153, 252). The count was wrong, not the platform. Re-measured against the sampled value it was still zero, so the finding survived -- but it survived by luck, not by the method","Running the same predicate over P40's macOS screenshot, which is full of blue tiles, and getting zero from that too","A colour predicate written from memory is a filter whose pattern is too narrow, and zero hits looks exactly like a clean result. Sample the actual pixel value from the image before counting, and run the predicate against an image KNOWN to contain the colour before trusting a zero. Same shape as gate 1 in the mistakes_prevention skill: the filter was silent, not wrong-looking"
2026-09-03,Verification,Judged a Win32Synthesiser change three times -- it regressed the working half; the redirect was broken; the background task was at fault -- and rebuilt between each judgement,"The binary never contained the replay at all. GtkBackend guards the ActionFileReplay call with #if SCUI_DEBUG and compile.zsh does not export SCUI_DEBUG; it only mixes the value into a hash that decides whether to drop SwiftPM caches. Every rebuild produced an executable with the replay compiled out. run.zsh printed NOTHING -- no error, no warning, no replaying line -- and the app started and rendered normally",Running the exe directly with an absolute path and still getting zero output. An app that starts and draws while its replay produces not one line is not a redirection problem,A gate that is written and never true is silent in both directions: the flag is accepted and the feature is absent. flow.md section 3a already records this exact shape from the Android work and I did not connect it for an hour. When a feature produces NO output at all rather than wrong output suspect it was compiled out before suspecting how it was invoked. Check with a non-interpolated literal from inside the guard
2026-09-03,Verification,The replay is not compiled into the binary -- strings finds zero occurrences of the log line it prints,It was compiled in the whole time. The log line is string INTERPOLATION so no contiguous literal survives compilation. Searching for non-interpolated fragments from the same function (geometry frame= and at layout scale) finds one each,"Adding a control: a literal that MUST be present. It was, which proved the search worked and the target was the wrong string",Second time today that a broken check invented a defect. A grep for a symbol that does not exist as a literal returns zero exactly like an absent feature does. Choose a search term the compiler cannot transform and pair it with a positive control in the same command
2026-09-03,Verification,"Verified the SCUI_DEBUG export fix by checking that the string geometry frame= appears in the binary -- it did, so the fix worked",The string proves nothing either way. It lives in ActionFileReplay.swift and InputEvent is an UNCONDITIONAL library target so it is compiled in both cases. What #if SCUI_DEBUG guards is the CALL in GtkBackend and a call is not a string. A build without the flag showed the same 1,"Running the negative case, which is the only reason it was caught. Without the flag the replay printed 0 lines; with it, 5. That is the check that discriminates","A false POSITIVE this time, which is worse than the two false negatives earlier today: it would have shipped a fix declared verified on evidence that could not distinguish fixed from broken. When a feature is switched on by a call rather than by code that contains a literal, no string search can test it -- run it and count the output. And run the negative case: a check that cannot fail has not passed"
2026-09-04,Diagnostics,"P1's first synthesised click is consumed: one click 0/3, the same click twice 3/3, a move then a click 0/3","The click always worked. The column was sheet OBSERVED, not sheet opened. Identity is checked before each action and never after the last one, and the fix earlier that day replaced finishReplay's ownWindow() call -- which dumped as a side effect -- with a visibleWindows() loop, deleting the only observation point after the final action. The two-click file was buying a second look, not a second press.","Adding one trailing sleep row so a check ran after the sheet mapped: one click, 3/3","A fix that removes a diagnostic is a change to what can be measured. Before believing a new negative, ask what the last fix stopped printing -- and make the check demonstrate it can still fail."
